{title: O the Deep, Deep Love of Jesus}
{artist: Samuel Trevor Francis}
{key: Dm}
{time: 8/4}
{tempo: 76}

Verse 1
[Dm]O the deep, deep [C]love of Jesus — [Dm]vast, unmeasured, [A]boundless, free,
[Dm]rolling as a [C]mighty ocean [Dm]in its fullness [A]over [Dm]me!
[F]Underneath me, [C]all around me, [Dm]is the current [C]of thy [F]love —
[Dm]leading onward, [C]leading homeward, [Dm]to thy glorious [A]rest a[Dm]bove.

Verse 2
[Dm]O the deep, deep [C]love of Jesus, spread His [Dm]praise from [A]shore to
[Dm]shore! How He [C]loveth, ever loveth, [Dm]changeth never, nevermore! [A]How [Dm]He
[F]watches o'er [C]His loved ones, [Dm]died to call them [C]all His [F]own; How
[Dm]for them [C]He intercedeth, [Dm]watcheth o'er them from [A]the throne!

Verse 3
[Dm]O the deep, deep love [C]of Jesus, love of [Dm]every love the [A]best! 'Tis
[Dm]an ocean full of [C]blessing, 'tis [Dm]a haven giving rest! [A]O [Dm]the
[F]deep, deep [C]love of Jesus, 'tis [Dm]a heav'n of heav'ns [C]to me; [F]And it lifts
[Dm]me up [C]to glory, for [Dm]it lifts me up [A]to Thee!
